74 "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/49/494158fe124fe1c8e1f7f618695dc9846991bd074b199a45a5874ddb8ad16e86.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=\\frac{34}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=\\frac{17 \\pi}{3} .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $\\frac{34}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{\\frac{34}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{34}{3}}^{2}}=\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{17 \\pi}{3}+\\frac{34 \\sqrt{2}}{3}=\\frac{17}{3}(\\pi+2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564665 1080 "\\frac{13 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{13 \\pi}{3}" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564665 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564665 1083 #uuid "315d6a3a-bf07-5695-aa6d-9283f74a6fb6" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564666 1080 "34" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564666 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564666 1083 #uuid "3458a9b8-cdbc-5786-bf2f-2b7ac0f4648d" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564667 1080 "22 + 11 \\pi" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564667 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564667 1083 #uuid "376127e0-f21c-5548-b2e1-55245e36fa29" 13194139536074 17592186045443 true] [17592186564668